module bindings.javascript.xml_crypto_signed_references_unused;

// `xml-crypto` splits an XML signature check into two questions, and its
// README is explicit that answering only the first is not enough: "The
// xml-crypto api requires you to supply it separately the xml signature and
// the signed xml (in checkSignature)". `SignedXml.checkSignature(xml)` returns
// whether *a* signature over *some* subset of that document verified; it does
// not say which subset. The library's own guidance after a successful check is
// `var signedBytes = sig.getSignedReferences();` followed by "It is now safe
// to load SAML, obtain the assertion XML, or do whatever else is needed. Be
// sure to only use authenticated data." It documents the older
// `getReferences()` as deprecated because "the content in them should be
// treated as unsigned", and says moving to `getSignedReferences()` "will help
// prevent future XML signature wrapping attacks".
//
// A module that constructs `SignedXml`, loads a signature into it with
// `loadSignature`, and calls `checkSignature` therefore has the verification
// half of the API and none of the attribution half. Whatever it hands on to
// assertion processing is a node it re-selected from the parsed document, so a
// response carrying a legitimately signed element beside an attacker-authored
// Assertion passes the boolean and delivers the attacker's assertion -- the
// signature-wrapping shape the SAML profile has been broken by repeatedly.
//
// The scope is the module rather than the function because the verification
// helper and the caller that consumes the signed bytes are conventionally
// separate functions in the same file, as they are in every wrapper around
// this API. Each name is matched as a whole `call:` token, so `getReferences`
// does not stand in for `getSignedReferences`. A module that reads the signed
// references anywhere satisfies the control and is not reported; so does one
// that only signs, since it never calls `checkSignature`.
binding xmlCryptoSignedReferencesUnused {
  query pattern presenceNode where node.scope == "module" and node.context.language == "javascript" and node.context.call == "SignedXml" and node.context.call == "loadSignature" and node.context.call == "checkSignature" and not (node.context.call == "getSignedReferences")
  emit issue code.SamlAssertionWrappingBypass at node
}
